  "result": "The plan is written to `<home>\\.claude\\plans\\add-a-new-parameter-velvety-cook.md`. The ExitPlanMode tool isn't available in this session, so I'm presenting it here for approval instead.\n\n**Plan: add `click.KeyValue`**\n\n1. **`src/click/types.py`**: add `class KeyValue(ParamType[tuple[str, str]])` after `UUIDParameterType`, with `name = \"key=value\"`.\n   - `convert` returns a tuple unchanged, so defaults work.\n   - Otherwise it uses `value.partition(\"=\")`, splitting on the first `=` so values may contain `=` and an empty value is allowed.\n   - If there is no `=` or the key is empty, it calls `self.fail(_(\"{value!r} is not a valid key=value pair.\"))`.\n2. **`src/click/__init__.py`**: export `KeyValue`.\n3. **`docs/api.md`**: add `autoclass:: KeyValue` to the Types section.\n4. **`CHANGES.md`**: add a changelog entry.\n5. **`tests/test_types.py`**:\n   - `a=b` gives `(\"a\", \"b\")`.\n   - `a=b=c` gives `(\"a\", \"b=c\")`.\n   - `a=` gives `(\"a\", \"\")`.\n   - `novalue` and `=v` fail with the expected message.\n   - The type works with `multiple=True`.\n\nVerification is `pytest tests/test_types.py tests/test_info_dict.py` plus the full suite.\n\nApprove the plan and I'll implement it, or tell me what to change first.",
